 fetch the data."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It will then cache the data using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'todos'"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchTodos"},{"type":"text","value":" as the unique identifiers for that cache."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook will mark itself as stale after the configured "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"staleTime"},{"type":"text","value":" (defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":", or immediately)."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A second instance of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)"},{"type":"text","value":" mounts elsewhere."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Because this exact data exists in the cache from the first instance of this query, that data is immediately returned from the cache."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A background refetch is triggered for both queries (but only one request), since a new instance appeared on screen."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both instances are updated with the new data if the fetch is successful"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both instances of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)"},{"type":"text","value":" query are unmounted and no longer in use."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Since there are no more active instances of this query, a cache timeout is set using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cacheTime"},{"type":"text","value":" to delete and garbage collect the query (defaults to "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5 minutes"}]},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before the cache timeout has completed another instance of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)"},{"type":"text","value":" mounts. The query immediately returns the available cached value while the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchTodos"},{"type":"text","value":" function is being run in the background to populate the query with a fresh value."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The final instance of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)"},{"type":"text","value":" unmounts."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No more instances of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)"},{"type":"text","value":" appear within "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5 minutes"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This query and its data are deleted and garbage collected."}]}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"basic-example","text":"Basic Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> Please thoroughly read the [Important Defaults](./important-defaults) before reading this guide\n\n## Basic Example\n\nThis caching example illustrates the story and lifecycle of:\n\n- Query Instances with and without cache data\n- Background Refetching\n- Inactive Queries\n- Garbage Collection\n\nLet's assume we are using the default `cacheTime` of **5 minutes** and the default `staleTime` of `0`.\n\n- A new instance of `useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)` mounts.\n  - Since no other queries have been made with this query + variable combination, this query will show a hard loading state and make a network request to fetch the data.\n  - It will then cache the data using `'todos'` and `fetchTodos` as the unique identifiers for that cache.\n  - The hook will mark itself as stale after the configured `staleTime` (defaults to `0`, or immediately).\n- A second instance of `useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)` mounts elsewhere.\n  - Because this exact data exists in the cache from the first instance of this query, that data is immediately returned from the cache.\n- A background refetch is triggered for both queries (but only one request), since a new instance appeared on screen.\n  - Both instances are updated with the new data if the fetch is successful\n- Both instances of the `useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)` query are unmounted and no longer in use.\n  - Since there are no more active instances of this query, a cache timeout is set using `cacheTime` to delete and garbage collect the query (defaults to **5 minutes**).\n- Before the cache timeout has completed another instance of `useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)` mounts. The query immediately returns the available cached value while the `fetchTodos` function is being run in the background to populate the query with a fresh value.\n- The final instance of `useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)` unmounts.\n- No more instances of `useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)` appear within **5 minutes**.\n  - This query and its data are deleted and garbage collected.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: caching\ntitle: Caching Examples\n---\n\n> Please thoroughly read the [Important Defaults](./important-defaults) before reading this guide\n\n## Basic Example\n\nThis caching example illustrates the story and lifecycle of:\n\n- Query Instances with and without cache data\n- Background Refetching\n- Inactive Queries\n- Garbage Collection\n\nLet's assume we are using the default `cacheTime` of **5 minutes** and the default `staleTime` of `0`.\n\n- A new instance of `useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)` mounts.\n  - Since no other queries have been made with this query + variable combination, this query will show a hard loading state and make a network request to fetch the data.\n  - It will then cache the data using `'todos'` and `fetchTodos` as the unique identifiers for that cache.\n  - The hook will mark itself as stale after the configured `staleTime` (defaults to `0`, or immediately).\n- A second instance of `useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)` mounts elsewhere.\n  - Because this exact data exists in the cache from the first instance of this query, that data is immediately returned from the cache.\n- A background refetch is triggered for both queries (but only one request), since a new instance appeared on screen.\n  - Both instances are updated with the new data if the fetch is successful\n- Both instances of the `useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)` query are unmounted and no longer in use.\n  - Since there are no more active instances of this query, a cache timeout is set using `cacheTime` to delete and garbage collect the query (defaults to **5 minutes**).\n- Before the cache timeout has completed another instance of `useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)` mounts. The query immediately returns the available cached value while the `fetchTodos` function is being run in the background to populate the query with a fresh value.\n- The final instance of `useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)` unmounts.\n- No more instances of `useQuery('todos', fetchTodos)` appear within **5 minutes**.\n  - This query and its data are deleted and garbage collected.\n"}
